
@startuml catan-progress

!include mda-style.puml
!include mda-patterns.puml

package "Aesthetics" as A <<aesthetics>> {
    $Luck()
    $Achievement()
    $AnalysisParalisis()
}

package "Dynamics" as D <<dynamics>> {
    $IncreasingRewards("main")
    $ResourceManagement()
}

package "Mechanics" as M <<mechanics>> {
    $Dice()
    $Resources()
    $Construction("main")
    $Territories()
    $Scores()
    $Randomness()
    $Cards()
    $Decks()
    $DrawingStacks()
    $Hands()
    $Upgrades()
}

randomness <-- dice

' dice dictates which resources produce, having resources allows you to put down more settlements/roads, which increases your territory. The territory you occupy also determines which resources you have access to

dice ..> resources
resources ..> construction
resources <.. upgrades
resources <.. territories

construction --> increasing_rewards
territories <-- construction
upgrades <-- construction
increasing_rewards --> achievement

'' resources enable resource management, which can also lead to analysis paralysis
resources --> resource_management
resource_management ..> analysis_paralisis
construction ..> analysis_paralisis


' cards are ararnged in to decks, which are piled into stacks which provide an element of randomness and therefore luck

cards --> decks
decks --> drawing_stacks
drawing_stacks --> randomness
randomness --> luck

'' your current resources are represented by cards and the current number of resorueces available modulates your hand

cards --> hands
hands <.. resources 

'' The number of things on the board directly affects the number of victory points you have 
construction ..> scores
scores --> achievement

' I am unsure how to model the fact that resources enable you to buy more development cards

' I would argue that one of the strongest sense of progressions comes from the central loop around construction and resources

'' I could also model something where the drawing stack itself modulates the score, as development cards allow you to earn points.

drawing_stacks ..> resources



@enduml

